From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: one file dialog, the one of Windows 10.

Programs had three dialogs: GetOpenFileName gave Windows 95's (Look in,
the places bar), IFileDialog (Chrome's Open and Save) Wine's half-done one
with a bare tree and three arrows, SHBrowseForFolder the old tree. Now all
of them get the Common Item Dialog as Windows 10 has it, as Arctic NT's
comdlg32 made it: back, forward and up, the address bar of folders with its
refresh, the search box; Organize, New folder and the view; the tree and the
files; the names and the buttons in a band at the bottom.

- itemdlg.c: Arctic NT's layout and commands (the history of the arrows,
  Organize's cut, copy, paste, select all, delete, rename, properties, New
  folder named in place, the views, the search that narrows the folder, the
  CDM_ messages of hooks, a hook's dialog in the band). Its parts are drawn
  by itemdlg_chrome.c in the look of the system: dark when the windows are,
  the round fields of Windows 11 when the visual style has that size,
  everything at the window's own DPI (a program aware of the monitors, as
  Chrome is, gets it sharp; WM_DPICHANGED moves it to another scale). The
  keys of Windows' dialog: Alt+Left, Alt+Right, Alt+Up, Backspace, F5,
  Alt+D, F4, Ctrl+E. SetFolder on a dialog on the screen goes there.
- filedlgofn.c: GetOpenFileName and GetSaveFileName through it, the
  OPENFILENAME in and out as documented; only Windows 3.1's look (a hook or
  several files without OFN_EXPLORER) keeps the old dialog, as in Windows.
- itemdlg_res.rc: its words in English, Ukrainian and Russian, in a block
  of string IDs of their own (comdlg32.rc takes its words from the po files).
- shell32/brsfolder.c: SHBrowseForFolder picks folders with it (32-bit
  programs; ReactOS's shell32 does the same for 64-bit ones).
- shell32/ebrowser.c: the roots of Windows 10's navigation pane: Desktop,
  Downloads, Documents, Pictures, This PC open, Network; whole rows.
- explorerframe/nstc.c: the tree takes the visual style's Explorer look, and the
  user's folders the names This PC has for them.
---
